# Refactored and simple

Do not grow a single `index.html` script. After each feature, extract until files stay small and one-purpose.

- **One concern per file:** `grid.js` is layout/order; `dialog.js` is overlays; `store.js` is JSON; `js/widgets/*.js` is one widget.
- **Pure functions** for math and clamps (delay, interval 1–900, max 4 widgets, max 5 sub-widgets). Those get unit tests. DOM stays thin.
- **Reuse chrome:** confirm + settings dialogs come from `dialog.js` + `dialog.css`. Never a one-off modal per widget.
- Delete dead code, unused CSS, and duplicate palettes. Rename when names lie.
- If a function needs a paragraph of comments, split it.

```js
// ❌ BAD — widget opens its own ad-hoc overlay
chime.querySelector('.gear').onclick = () => {
  document.body.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', '<div class="c-modal">…');
};

// ✅ GOOD — shared dialog; widget only supplies fields + onSave
openSettings({ title: 'Chime', body, onSave: saveChime });
```
